    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1733">

                <pb facs="1247" n="1131" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 718.1915/234.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hale to the Secretary of State.</hi><anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1733-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 58.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I have
                    received an important communication from the Minister for Foreign Affairs, dated
                    January 14, concerning the boundary dispute between Costa Rica and Panama, a
                    copy of which and its enclosures, together with translations of all, I enclose,
                    marked Enclosure No. 1.</p>
                <p>A copy of my reply, dated January 21, is also enclosed, marked Enclosure No.
                    2.</p>
                <p>In this connection I respectfully ask for instructions as to my further
                    procedure.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Hale.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>







